  "title": "Checkerboard m-sequence-based c-VEP dataset from",
  "description": "A derivative EEG dataset containing checkerboard m-sequence-based code-modulated visual evoked potential (c-VEP) recordings from 16 healthy participants across 8 sessions. The dataset evaluates the influence of spatial frequency in visual stimuli for brain-computer interface applications, with 16-channel EEG data sampled at 256 Hz using a standard 10-05 montage. This resource supports benchmarking and development of c-VEP-based BCI systems.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were acquired from 16 healthy participants using 16 channels at 256 Hz sampling rate with a standard 1005 montage and 50 Hz line frequency. Each participant completed 8 sessions with 3 runs per session (2 training, 1 testing). Visual stimuli consisted of checkerboard m-sequence patterns presented in a two-class c-VEP paradigm.",
